# Helm charts

Charts live under `helm_charts/`: `gateway`, `redis`, `metabase`, `care_be`, `care_fe`, `dcm4chee`. Terraform owns releases in `deploy/helm.tf`.

When adding a chart, scaffold first, then trim and adapt:

```bash
helm create helm_charts/<name>
```

Delete default templates you do not need (Ingress, HPA, extra Service, `tests/`, `NOTES.txt`, unused ServiceAccount, and similar). Keep and reshape the remaining Deployment/Service (and helpers) to match this repo: Gateway API (`httproute.yaml`, `backend-policy.yaml`) instead of Ingress, checksum annotations, explicit requests/limits and probes. Legacy GCE Ingress is `enable_legacy_ingress` only.

Then:

1. Define values as a local in `deploy/helm-values.tf` and pass them with `yamlencode()` on `helm_release`, merged with `common_helm_values`.
2. Add image/replica fields to `var.helm_config` in root `variables.tf` and `environments/sample.tfvars`.

Terraform injects:

```yaml
global:
  cloudProvider: gcp
  namespace: <namespace>
  gateway:
    name: care-regional-gateway
    namespace: <namespace>
    gatewayClassName: gke-l7-regional-external-managed
  backendPolicy:
    enabled: true
    securityPolicy: <cloud-armor-policy-name>
  httpRoute:
    enabled: true
```

Charts should read `global.*` for routing and backend policy. Secrets via `envFromSecret` pointing at `deploy/secrets.tf`. Do not revive `deploy/generated_values/` (disabled).

Full detail: `.github/instructions/helm.instructions.md`.
